    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0123" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg29"/>

                <head>No. 27.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tree
                        to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 4, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 186.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith the
                    correspondence with the Belgian minister of foreign affairs on the subject of
                    the proposed visit of the Gate City Guard, of Atlanta, to Belgium.</p>
                <p>The Prince de Chimay, in his note informing me that the Government accords the
                    authorization requested by the Guard, observes that “the best welcome will be
                    reserved for them.”</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lambert Tree</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d27-a1.xml" xpointer="d27-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d27-a2.xml" xpointer="d27-a2"/>
